# Research data supplied by the author, not redistributed from this repository.
# The record words are Keranen / Gavrilenko's; word-anatomy.js verifies them
# locally and every consumer skips cleanly when they are absent.
datasets/keranen_*.txt
keranen_*.txt

# `papers/` holds two different kinds of thing, and they must not share a rule.
#
#   papers/<anything>      LOCAL third-party literature. Copyrighted, cited in
#                          MATH_CLAIMS.md by identifier, never redistributed
#                          from this repository. Ignored.
#   papers/paperN/         a PROJECT-OWNED canonical paper package (manuscript,
#                          figures, audit, reproducibility). Repository content.
#
# Until 2026-08-31 a blanket `papers/` rule covered both. papers/paper4/ was
# tracked only by grandfathering -- git ignores untracked files, not tracked
# ones -- so the rule silently would have swallowed papers/paper5/ and every
# package after it. Ignore everything directly under papers/, then re-include
# the numbered project-owned directories.
#
# The trailing slash on the exceptions is load-bearing: it matches directories
# only, so a third-party file whose name happens to start with "paper" (say
# papers/paper1992_survey.pdf) can never be re-included by it. The digit class
# is a second guard on the same point.
papers/*
!papers/paper[0-9]*/
!papers/paper[0-9]*/**

latest/*.pdf

# PDFs are ignored by default, because third-party literature arrives as PDF.
# The exceptions are the project's own canonical and reader-facing artifacts,
# and they must come after the general rule to take effect -- a later pattern
# wins. Without them a project-owned paper PDF would be invisible to git while
# looking perfectly present on disk.
*.pdf
!papers/paper[0-9]*/**/*.pdf
!publications/**/*.pdf

# Personal research notes and correspondence, not for redistribution.
teoria/

# Mirrored copy of a third party's (Veikko Keranen) personal homepage.
# Not this project's content; never redistribute.
nettisivu/

# Personal correspondence, not for redistribution.
whatsapp_transcript.txt

# Local cache of extension-depth tables (table-library.js). Regenerable by
# construction and large; every record carries its own checksum and provenance,
# so a missing cache costs time, never correctness.
tables/

# Derived from MATH_CLAIMS.md by claims-export.js. Regenerate, never edit.
claims.json
node_modules/
